1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:09,840
Today, most scientific research is funded by government grants, companies doing research and development, and non-profit foundations.
如今，大多数科学研究由政府拨款、从事研发的企业和非营利基金会资助。

2
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:15,910
As a society, we reap the rewards from this science, but we also help pay for it.
我们整个社会从这些科学研究中收获回报，但也在为它出一份钱。

3
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:23,540
You indirectly support science through taxes you pay, products and services you purchase, and donations you make.
你通过缴纳税款、购买产品和服务以及捐款，间接地支持着科学。

4
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,800
Funding for science has changed with the times.
对科学的资助随着时代发生了变化。

5
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:35,430
Historically, science has been largely supported through private patronage, church sponsorship, or simply paying for the research yourself.
历史上，支撑科学的主要是私人资助、教会赞助，或者干脆自己掏钱做研究。

6
00:00:36,230 --> 00:00:43,810
Today, researchers are likely to be funded by a mix of grants from various government agencies, institutions, and foundations.
如今，研究人员很可能由多方拨款共同资助，这些拨款来自各类政府部门、机构和基金会。

7
00:00:44,610 --> 00:00:47,400
Other research is funded by private companies.
另一些研究则由私营企业资助。

8
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,430
Such corporate sponsorship is widespread in some fields.
这种企业赞助在一些领域很普遍。

9
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:58,420
Almost 75% of U.S. clinical trials in medicine are paid for by private companies.
美国近75%的医学临床试验由私营企业出资。

10
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:05,000
And, of course, some researchers today still fund small-scale studies out of their own pockets.
当然，如今也仍有一些研究人员自掏腰包，资助小规模的研究。

11
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:14,910
Most of us can’t afford to do nuclear research as a private hobby, but birdwatchers, rock collectors, and others can do real research on a limited budget.
我们大多数人负担不起把核研究当作私人爱好来做，但观鸟者、岩石收藏者等人可以在预算有限的情况下开展真正的研究。

12
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:21,880
In a perfect world, money wouldn’t matter—all scientific studies would be completely objective.
在理想的世界里，金钱无关紧要——所有科学研究都会完全客观。

13
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:26,100
But in the real world, funding may introduce biases.
但在现实世界中，资助可能会带来偏差。

14
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:37,990
Drug research sponsored by the pharmaceutical industry is more likely to end up favoring the drug under consideration than studies sponsored by government grants or charitable organizations.
与政府拨款或慈善组织资助的研究相比，由制药业赞助的药物研究最终更有可能偏向所研究的药物。

15
00:01:38,790 --> 00:01:48,130
Similarly, nutrition research sponsored by the food industry is more likely to end up favoring the food under consideration than independently funded research.
同样，与独立资助的研究相比，由食品行业赞助的营养研究最终更有可能偏向所研究的食品。

16
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:50,710
So what should we make of all this?
那么，我们该如何看待这一切呢？

17
00:01:51,510 --> 00:01:55,840
Should we ignore any research funded by companies or special interest groups?
我们应该无视所有由企业或特殊利益集团资助的研究吗？

18
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,640
Certainly not.
当然不应该。

19
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:02,280
These groups provide invaluable funding for scientific research.
这些企业和团体为科学研究提供着极其宝贵的资金。

20
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:09,500
Furthermore, science has many safeguards in place to catch instances of bias that affect research outcomes.
此外，科学界已设有许多保障机制，用来查出影响研究结果的偏差情况。

21
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:16,420
Ultimately, misleading results will be corrected as science proceeds; however, this process takes time.
随着科学向前推进，误导性的结果最终会得到纠正；不过，这一过程需要时间。

22
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:23,240
Meanwhile, it pays to examine studies funded by industry or special interest groups with extra care.
在此期间，值得格外仔细地审视由产业界或特殊利益集团资助的研究。

23
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:27,470
Are the results consistent with independently funded studies?
这些研究的结果与独立资助的研究结果一致吗？

24
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:31,200
What do other scientists have to say about this research?
其他科学家对这些研究有何看法？

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:38,290
A little examination can go a long way towards identifying bias associated with the funding source.
稍加审视，就能在很大程度上帮助识别与资金来源相关的偏差。
